  "scientific_review": [
    "All 14 declared fixed-latitude windows at January 15 and July 15, 2022 00Z are retained as 28 original section/date cases. Exact cloud profile bytes, native coordinates and global indices, hyperslabs, timestamps, attributes, masks, all candidate scores and local peaks, selected columns and threshold layers remain traceable. No unsuccessful or censored case is omitted.",
    "Frozen latitude v2 collection, geometry, bounded target-budget ledger and exact zonal reader, component/selection/connected-layer helpers are unchanged. Forty-five cloud tests passed in groups 12/11/5/5/8/4, followed by recomputation and audit of every retained section. Exact failed-component retries reserve future first attempts, do not replay successful other fields, and remain within original cell/byte caps. The ledger records actual requested shapes and returned arrays; it does not claim wire traffic or source wire hashes.",
    "Both currents use fixed 0-degree northward components through depth, primary 10 cm/s, surface >5 cm/s and complete finite upper-200-m signed-integral selection. First western native index breaks ties. Incomplete shallow shelf support, no qualifying flow, selected edge/support-edge maxima and primary-depth censoring remain explicit. No gate, direction, cutoff or selected-profile replacement is tuned after outcomes. Broad geographic maxima do not independently establish named-current, water-mass or branch identity.",
    "Irminger scope is partial 56–65 N western Reykjanes Ridge. Fresh Fried and de Jong (2022) publisher text describes two surface-intensified cores, intermediate return flow and deeper northward IC water. One selected maximum can switch between cores and is neither their sum nor a tracked coherent axis. A connected model contour may mix upper and deeper water masses. Return toward Greenland, North Icelandic continuation, interior gyre, opposite ridge-side flow and detached eddies remain separate target identities/contamination risks.",
    "West Spitsbergen scope is partial 73–79.6 N northward slope corridor with an original 77.25 N section. The selected departure and stop gates are editorial conventions. Front Current, Barents inflow, recirculation, shelf/fjord intrusions and downstream branches are separate targets. Spitsbergen Atlantic naming remains unresolved and is not merged. No Atlantic Water temperature/salinity gate is applied; source water-mass thresholds are not silently transferred to HYCOM in-situ temperature/practical salinity.",
    "Fresh Dundas and Fer (2026) methods describe geostrophic shear referenced to satellite surface velocities, replacing anomalous glider DAC consistently across sections. Existing CC BY 4.0 archive metadata provides hydrography and depth-averaged currents, not a ready-made vertical velocity profile. No glider/altimetry field retrieval or author-profile reconstruction is performed here. The 1,000-m glider limit, 20–500-m averaging and selected-core width statistic are not physical current bottoms or compatible whole-current dimensions. Observational reconstruction remains a separate validation lead.",
    "All windows are exploratory OSW geography, not digitized axes, measured widths, source isobaths or uncertainty bands. All ocean-field acquisition, retries, geometry/selection/contour calculations and tests ran sequentially in the cloud on one idle CPU. Local work reviewed text/metadata, prepared code, verified hashes and retained exact artifacts. No local numerical ocean-field processing/tests or runtime/UI/browser work occurred. Fixed publication and transport caps remain unchanged.",
    "Two exact snapshots do not establish monthly means, annual ranges, seasonal envelopes, confidence intervals or independent observations. Threshold lower depths and paired spans remain qualified regional model diagnostics, not physical current thickness or water-mass boundaries. Canonical register v48, projection inventory v9 and the 102-size-reference eddy baseline remain unchanged by source retention. No full physical route depth, matched width-depth area, volume, state join or global total is admitted. All original source sections and gaps must survive projection."
